From fb97be7e6075da25f5216b20cafc68a3206dde11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] refactor(backend): shared connection pool, design
 patterns, Swagger docs, bug fixes

Database
- One NpgsqlDataSource (singleton, single physical pool) + AddDbContextPool.
  DbContext deliberately NOT a singleton: it isn't thread-safe and is shared by
  concurrent requests and the background scheduler.
- Startup schema bootstrap moved verbatim from Program.cs to DatabaseInitializer.

Patterns
- IPatientAccessService replaces 6 copy-pasted access queries.
- Domain/DoseSchedule is the single source of scheduling rules (was duplicated
  in DoseService and NotificationScheduler).
- ApiControllerBase (CurrentUserId), GlobalExceptionHandler (problem+json with
  'message'), ServiceRegistration/SwaggerRegistration extension methods.

Swagger
- XML docs on every controller, action, service, entity and contract; response
  codes via ProducesResponseType; served in Development or when Swagger:Enabled=true.

Fixes
- Undo after Take now restores medicine supply (supply drifted down).
- GET /doses and PUT /patient no longer 500 for users with several patients.
- Malformed dates in reschedule/pause/medicine/patient now return 400, not 500.
- Family search/member photos return signed URLs (were raw storage keys).
- History medicine-name filter is case-insensitive (ILIKE).
- Password reset links are no longer written to production logs.
- Doses include ActionedByName so caregivers see who recorded a dose.
- New POST /api/notifications/read-all.

Tests: updated for new constructor; added Undo supply, multi-patient, schedule
rules, time zone fallback and connection-string tests.
