From fa7e738fd40bf5a225da0b69ca51a748406788fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:43:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] feat(api): dose- and medicine-level rescheduling with
 care-team notifications

- POST /api/doses/{id}/reschedule now takes date + time: the original becomes
  'rescheduled' (RescheduleTo + RescheduleToTime) and a NEW pending dose is created at
  the target, linked via RescheduledFromId (previously nothing was created, so moved
  doses vanished). Validates future target, free slot, not already recorded.
- Undo on a moved original removes the moved dose (allowed while it is still open).
- GET /api/doses includes moved-in doses and returns rescheduledFrom date/time.
- POST /api/medicine-actions/{id}/reschedule: new times from an effective date; old
  record ends (EndedOn), replacement keeps supply/settings, cycle alignment and remaining
  course length, with RescheduledFromId + PreviousTimes for the 'Rescheduled' mark.
- Scheduler sends reminders/due/missed alerts for moved doses (shared ProcessReminders).
- ICareTeamNotifier: in-app + push to owner and approved family (dose_rescheduled,
  schedule_changed).
- Schema: 5 nullable columns added idempotently at startup.
- Tests: reschedule creates/links dose, undo removes it, no past targets, EndedOn rule.
